              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">  Compute exploration score </span><math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">b</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> from complexity and uncertainty
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">  Set token-level temperature </span><math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> and noise </span><math id="alg2.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l7.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">  Sample token predictions and keep the most confident positions
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">end</span><span id="alg2.l9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg2.l9.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l10.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Decode tokens to motion using the VQ-VAE decoder
</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4. </span>Experiments</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate DynMask on HumanML3D and KIT-ML, comparing against representative methods from multiple generation paradigms.
We then conduct systematic ablations to isolate the contribution of each design choice, analyze where the improvements concentrate across motion complexity levels, and validate the results through qualitative comparison and a user study.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1. </span>Setup</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Datasets.</span>
We evaluate on three standard motion datasets.
<span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">HumanML3D</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al., 2022</a>)</cite> is our main benchmark and provides paired motion-text examples with the standard train/val/test split.
<span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">KIT-ML</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Plappert et al., 2016</a>)</cite> serves as a second benchmark with different motion and language statistics.
We also use <span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">BABEL</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Punnakkal et al., 2021</a>)</cite> for cross-dataset transfer analysis.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metrics.</span>
Following standard text-to-motion evaluation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, we report R-Precision at top-1, top-2, and top-3, Fréchet Inception Distance (<span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FID</span>), Multimodal Distance (<span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MM-Dist</span>), Diversity, and MModality when available.
All metrics are computed using the standard motion and text feature extractors used in prior work.
We report averages over repeated evaluations, and confidence intervals are shown in the tables.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Implementation details.</span>
The <span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">core model</span> of DynMask consists of complexity-aware mask selection and motion-aware attention.
The <span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">full model</span> additionally includes complexity-aware decoding at inference time.
All main experiments use the same default hyperparameters unless a specific ablation states otherwise.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2. </span>Quantitative results</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare DynMask with representative methods from different generation paradigms on HumanML3D and KIT-ML.
Our main scope is masked motion generation, while other paradigms are included for broader context.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 1</span>. </span><span id="S4.T1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Comparison on HumanML3D.<span id="S4.T1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Methods are grouped by generation paradigm.
Our main scope is improvement within the masked motion generation family, while other paradigms are reported for broader context.
Blue background indicates the best and second-best generated results.</span></span></figcaption>
<table id="S4.T1.6" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T1.6.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T1.6.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S4.T1.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Method</span></th>
<td id="S4.T1.6.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S4.T1.6.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Top-1<math id="S4.T1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.6.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S4.T1.6.1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Top-2<math id="S4.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.6.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S4.T1.6.1.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Top-3<math id="S4.T1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
